node_modules/
out/
# ...except the benchmark RESULTS. out/ is ignored because it holds build output, recordings
# and frames — regenerable bulk. out/bench is the opposite: manifests, per-arm archived
# appmaps and the measured token/cost figures, none of which can be recreated without
# re-running the passes that produced them (~$45 for phase 1 alone, hours of fleet time).
# 472K as of 2026-08-01. Recordings and step frames stay ignored — those live under
# out/recording and out/runs.
!out/bench/
!out/bench/**
# out/bench-backup: snapshots of benchmark passes that were killed and re-run. "We started over"
# is the moment the previous attempt's numbers stop being reproducible, and a superseded pass is
# still the only evidence of what the code did before the fix that superseded it.
!out/bench-backup/
!out/bench-backup/**
#
# NOTE on how these exceptions actually work: `out/` above excludes the DIRECTORY, and git does
# not descend into an excluded directory, so none of the `!out/...` lines are ever evaluated for
# an untracked file. They document intent; the tracked files under out/bench and out/bench-backup
# were force-added (`git add -f`) and stay tracked because gitignore does not apply to files git
# already knows about. Adding a NEW result file needs `-f` too.
#
# TRACKED: out/archive/bench/<date>/ — the benchmark manifest family (manifest.json, the per-arm
# appmap copies, narrative.md). Kilobytes, and unrecreatable without re-running the passes that
# produced them. The ARCHIVE copy is what git holds rather than the live one, deliberately: the
# live directory is written to continuously while a pass runs, so tracking it means half-written
# manifests in commits. The two are hard links to the same inodes, so this costs nothing extra.
#
# NOT TRACKED: out/live/<runKey>/ and out/archive/<runKey>/ — the runs themselves. Step frames
# and recordings are gigabytes of PNGs and mp4s per pass. Git is not the backup mechanism for
# those; the hard-linked archive is.
.env
.playwright-mcp/
.DS_Store
CLAUDE.md
tools/winrec
*.bak

# Swift sidecar build artifacts
native/axdom
native/liveview
native/default-browser
tmp/
dist-electron

# Fleet credentials: the private SSH key for every Mac in hosts.json, plus the team
# OpenRouter key. Distributed with the app, never through git.
team-credentials.json
*.pem
id_ed25519*

# Holds a live OpenRouter key today. Already covered by David's personal ~/.config/git/ignore,
# which is exactly the problem: a teammate who clones this repo does not have that file, and
# the protection would silently not exist for them.
.claude/settings.local.json
.env.*

# Full checkouts made by agent worktrees. Several hundred MB, and each one carries its own
# copy of everything above — including files this list exists to keep out.
.claude/worktrees/
# Python bytecode from the render/fit scripts.
__pycache__/

# Source corpora for the cursor motion fit. The render path reads only the fitted outputs
# (data/motion-constants.json, data/motion-segments.json); these are needed solely to re-run
# scripts/fit-motion.py. 185MB, kept out of history deliberately.
data/cursor-keyboard-dataset-2026-07-30/
data/cursor-smoothed-dataset/

# Backups the claude-use-subscription script writes beside settings.local.json —
# same secret-bearing content as the ignored original, so they must never track.
.claude/settings.local.json.bak-*

# Frozen dash snapshots (./run dash:snapshot) — a metadata-only copy of a pass, built to be
# COPYied into a container image. The manifests inside are worth keeping, but they are already
# tracked at their source under out/bench; this is a derived, regenerable duplicate of them
# plus 800-odd run logs, and the deploy path that needs it (docs/deploying-the-dash.md) builds
# the image locally and pushes it, so the bytes never need to travel through git.
# A build-from-repo deploy is the exception and needs `git add -f snapshots/<name>`.
snapshots/
